Strength. Care. Growth

A1 Competence Delivery Center is a vital component of A1's telecommunications business. Acting as an expertise hub, CDC is dedicated in delivering full range of high-quality IT, network, financial and HR to support A1's operations across all OpCos, independent of location.

Using the power of A1 Group and leveraging bynergies, CDC enables transparency of resources, key skills and knowledge expansion and personal career growth opportunities’, paired with job stability. will

You will know we are the right place for you, if you are driven by:


 * Opportunities to learn and build your career;
 * Meaningful work in a stable and fast-paced company;
 * Diversity of people, projects, and platforms;
 * A supportive, fun, and inspiring place to work.



Would you like to join us?

Junior IP Data Center and Security Engineer

As a Junior Network Engineer at A1 Competence Delivery Center, you will gain hands-on experience in telecommunications and IT infrastructure, working with skilled engineers on real projects in an international environment. This entry-level role focuses on learning, mentorship, and practical involvement in deploying and maintaining network solutions.

You’ll assist with service migrations, configuration changes, and troubleshooting, while building your knowledge of core networking concepts. This is a great opportunity for those passionate about networking and eager to start a successful career as part of a supportive, growth-oriented team.

Your Daily Routine Would Include


 * Get involved in international projects and activities with guidance from senior engineers;
 * Assist in deploying and supporting new network solutions and customer services;
 * Assist in documenting network changes and troubleshooting steps;
 * Assist in troubleshooting basic network issues;
 * Learn to perform service migrations and configuration changes;
 * Work closely with experienced team members, field engineers, and other technical teams;
 * Receive hands-on training and mentoring in real environments.



We’ll know you can make it if you have:


 * Strong interest in IP networking, including core concepts like Switching, VLANs, STP, and basic Routing protocols;
 * Participation in networking courses (Cisco, Checkpoint, Fortinet, Palo Alto, or similar) is considered an advantage;
 * Good communication skills in English, both written and spoken;
 * German language is a plus;
 * Willingness to learn new technologies and continuously improve;
 * Ability to work in a team and adapt to dynamic environment;



Our gratitude for the job done will be eternal, but we’ll also offer you:


 * Innovative technologies and platforms to “play” with;
 * Modern working environment for your comfort;
 * Friendly, ambitious, and motivated teammates to support each other;
 * Thousands of online and in-person learning opportunities to grow;
 * Challenging assignments and career development opportunities in multinational environment;
 * Attractive remuneration package;
 * Flexible working schedule and opportunity for home office;
 * Numerous additional goodies, including, but not limited to free A1 services, discounts, health insurance and services, sports center, childcare, team and family events, etc.



You want to learn more? See us in action in our A1 Blog.

Sounds good? Apply now!

Deadline for applications: 11 August 2025

Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.

Any questions? Contact Яна Младенова

We are seeking a highly skilled and proactive Senior Corporate Security Engineer to join our cybersecurity team. The ideal candidate will drive secure configuration and operation of key endpoint and mobility systems – DLP, MDM, BYOD/VDI, and EDR – while coordinating closely with SOC, Data Protection, and Corporate Security functions. The role will also include leading security awareness initiatives and contributing to continuous improvement of our overall security posture.

This position offers a growth path toward a Corporate Security Team Lead role. Prior team leadership experience is considered a plus.

Responsibilities


 * Manage and optimize the organization’s Data Loss Prevention (DLP) systems to safeguard sensitive information;
 * Configure and maintain DLP systems in line with SOC, Data Protection, and Corporate Security requirements;
 * Monitor performance and adjust policies to improve data visibility and reduce false positives;
 * Coordinate with the MDM Team implementation, configuration, and maintenance of Mobile Device Management (MDM) and BYOD solutions;
 * Develop and enforce secure BYOD configurations and access controls;
 * Create and maintain baseline configurations for VDI environments supporting secure remote access;
 * Support the tuning of EDR solutions to enhance detection capabilities;
 * Manage endpoint asset inventory and ensure accurate software/service tracking;
 * Support SOC and Data Protection teams as an implementation partner;
 * Collaborate cross-functionally with IT, Legal, Risk, and Compliance;
 * Lead the development and execution of security training programs, campaigns, and awareness initiatives to foster a strong security culture;
 * Conduct periodic assessments of security policies and operational practices;
 * Ensure ongoing compliance with regulatory and industry frameworks (e.g., ISO 27001, NIST, DORA)




Requirememts:


 * 4+ years of experience in corporate IT or cybersecurity engineering;
 * Proven hands-on experience with DLP, MDM, BYOD/VDI, and EDR systems and tools;
 * Strong understanding of security principles and practices, particularly in endpoint, mobile, and remote-access security;
 * Hands-on experience with implementing and managing security awareness programs;
 * Build and maintain automation scripts and microservices in Python;
 * Familiarity with security frameworks and compliance standards (e.g., ISO 27001, NIST, PCI DSS);
 * Knowledge of mobile security, encryption technologies, and secure device management;
 * Proactive problem-solver with excellent communication skills;
 * Fluent in English




Nice to have:


 * Experience leading or mentoring a technical team;
 * Exposure to cross-functional policy development or GRC programs




What you will get in return:


 * Competitive Salary: We believe great work deserves great pay! Your skills and talents will be rewarded with a salary that makes you feel valued and motivated;
 * Work-Life Harmony: Join a company that genuinely cares about you—because your life outside of work matters just as much as your time on the clock;
 * Annual Performance Bonus: Your hard work doesn’t go unnoticed! Celebrate your achievements with a well-deserved annual bonus tied to your performance;
 * Generous Time Off: Need a breather? Our annual leave policy lets you recharge and enjoy life outside of work without a worry;
 * Employee Referral Program: Love working here? Share the love! Bring your talented friends on board and get rewarded for growing our awesome team;
 * Comprehensive Health & Pension Benefits: From medical insurance to pension plans, we’ve got your back. Plus, location-specific benefits and perks!;
 * Workation Wonderland: Live your digital nomad dreams with 30 extra days to work remotely from anywhere in the world (some restrictions apply). Adventure awaits!;
 * Volunteer Days: Make a difference! Take two additional paid days each year to support causes you care about and give back to the community




Be a key player at the forefront of the digital assets movement, propelling your career to new heights! Join a dynamic and rapidly expanding company that values and rewards talent, initiative, and creativity. Work alongside one of the most brilliant teams in the industry.

Acronis is a world leader in cyber protection—empowering people by providing them with cutting-edge technology that enables them to monitor, control, and protect the data that their businesses and lives depend on. We are looking for а Tier 3 QA Engineer who is ready to join our mission in creating a #CyberFit future!

In this role you will be responsible for verifying product functionality based on Customer reports, including designing test scenarios & running these tests, creating environments, analyzing test results, and preparing reports on the defects to the development/product team. In addition, you will participate in pre-release testing - conducting internal user acceptance testing prior to releases.

What You'll Do


 * Analyze Customers' issues, investigate root causes;
 * Identify test conditions, design test cases, plan testing activities;
 * Maintain and design complex test environments required for tests execution;
 * Execute test cases according to the described scenarios (Customer cases);
 * Work with logs & diagnostic information using appropriate techniques & tools;
 * Analyze test results, logs & prepare reports to the development teams;
 * Log & document bugs in the tracking system (Jira), verify bugs;
 * Participate in building of virtual testing framework;
 * Execute exploratory testing & User Acceptance Testing (UAT);
 * Collect comprehensive & relevant data for bug investigation;
 * Work with R&D, Support, Product, and other departments on technical questions & user scenarios.



What You Bring


 * Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or Engineering;
 * 2+ years of experience as a QA Tester (Manual) or System Administrator or in a related field;
 * Pre-Intermediate level of English (ability to read documentation & write simple texts) or higher;
 * Familiarity with any Virtualization system (VMWare ESXi, MS Hyper-V, oVirt, KVM);
 * Strong skills of basic Windows/Linux system operations, including software installation, network configuration, general troubleshooting;
 * Knowledge of various operating systems: MS Windows (including corporate versions) and Linux distributions;
 * Hands-on experience with GUI, and CLI;
 * Experience in testing or support of endpoint security solutions;
 * Experience in investigating and troubleshooting performance related incidents with built-in and 3rd-party tools.
 * Understanding of User Experience;
 * Understanding of common software failures & faults;
 * Attention to details;
 * Strong analytical & problem solving skills;
 * Time-management skills (SLA);
 * Strong multitasking;
 * Ability to work autonomously & in a team.



Would be considered plus if you have


 * MacOS experience;
 * Cybersecurity analyst's skills;
 * Scripting skills (e.g. JavaScript, Python, PowerShell, etc.).
 * Please submit your resume and application in English



Who We Are

Acronis is a global cyber protection company that provides natively integrated cybersecurity, data protection, and endpoint management for managed service providers (MSPs), small and medium businesses (SMBs), enterprise IT departments and home users. Our all-in-one solutions are highly efficient and designed to identify, prevent, detect, respond, remediate, and recover from modern cyberthreats with minimal downtime, ensuring data integrity and business continuity. We offer the most comprehensive security solution on the market for MSPs with our unique ability to meet the needs of diverse and distributed IT environments.

A Swiss company founded in Singapore in 2003, Acronis offers over twenty years of innovation with 15 offices worldwide and more than 1800 employees in 50+ countries. Acronis Cyber Protect is available in 26 languages in 150 countries and is used by over 20,000 service providers to protect over 750,000 businesses.

Our corporate culture is focused on making a positive impact on the lives of each employee and the communities we serve. Mutual trust, respect and belief that we can contribute to the world everyday are the cornerstones of our team. Each member of our “A-Team” plays an instrumental role in driving the success of our innovative and expanding business. We seek individuals who excel in dynamic, global environments and have a never give up attitude, contributing to our collective growth and impact.

Our Interview Practices

To maintain a fair and genuine hiring process, we kindly ask that all candidates participate in interviews without the assistance of AI tools or external prompts. Our interview process is designed to assess your individual skills, experiences, and communication style. We value authenticity and want to ensure we’re getting to know you—not a digital assistant. To help maintain this integrity, we ask to remove virtual backgrounds and include in-person interviews in our hiring process.

Use of AI-generated responses or third-party support during live interviews may be grounds for disqualification from the recruitment process and a full criminal, education and identification background check is required for all new hires.

Acronis is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, color, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, medical condition, protected veteran status, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances.

